      ---
      UEB Listener
      ---


UEB Listener

    The UEB Listener is a daemon that listens for notifications from SDC, posted to UEB (Universal Event Bus).
    On receipt of an event, the UEB listener downloads any artifacts posted and examines them to determine if
    the format (the outer XML tag) matches a supported format.  If so, it posts the file to the ASDC-API REST
    API in order to update the SDN-C database.

File Locations

    * Root directory : /opt/app/ueb-listener

    * Log files : /opt/app/ueb-listener/logs

    * Incoming files to be processed : /opt/app/ueb-listener/spool/asdc/incoming

    * Files already processed : /opt/app/ueb-listener/spool/asdc/archive




Tracing

    Each SDC notification creates a CONSUMER span using the Kafka traceparent and tracestate headers
    preserved by distribution client 2.4.0. Notifications without a valid parent start independent traces.
    The active context is propagated to SDN-C RESTCONF requests. HTTP client spans can be supplied
    by a Java agent; the listener itself injects context without creating duplicate HTTP spans.

    The standalone listener initializes OpenTelemetry and exports traces over OTLP HTTP/protobuf using
    the JDK HTTP transport. Configure the collector with OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT (or
    OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT). Use its HTTP/protobuf port (normally 4318); gRPC export
    requires a different sender. The default service name is sdnc-ueb-listener; override it with
    OTEL_SERVICE_NAME. Standard OpenTelemetry environment variables and Java system properties apply,
    including OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER and OTEL_SDK_DISABLED. Metrics and log export are disabled by default.
    The SDK flushes and shuts down when the JVM exits. If an OpenTelemetry Java agent has already
    registered a global provider, the listener reuses it instead of initializing another SDK.
